# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[codz]
*$py.class

# C extensions
*.so

# Distribution / packaging
#
# Anchored to the repo root, deliberately. The stock Python .gitignore leaves
# these unanchored, and `lib/` then matches at ANY depth — which silently
# excluded `frontend/src/lib/`, i.e. the entire wire contract, from two
# commits that claimed to add it. `git add -A` says nothing when a path is
# ignored.
#
# `dist/` is gone from this list. It used to be unanchored on purpose, to
# catch `frontend/dist` as well as sdist output — but the built SPA now lives
# at `app/dist` and is COMMITTED (see app/client/.gitignore for why), and an
# unanchored `dist/` would silently ignore it.
# `scripts/build_model_wheel.py` writes to `build/wheels`, which `/build/`
# above already covers, so nothing else wants this name.
.Python
/build/
/develop-eggs/
/downloads/
/eggs/
/.eggs/
/lib/
/lib64/
/parts/
/sdist/
/var/
/wheels/

# The built SPA, at the app root — see app/client/.gitignore for why it is
# tracked at all. Sourcemaps are the one part that is not: 5.1 MB against
# 1.2 MB for the bundle, regenerated on every build.
/app/dist/**/*.map
/share/python-wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# PyInstaller
#   Usually these files are written by a python script from a template
#   before PyInstaller builds the exe, so as to inject date/other infos into it.
*.manifest
*.spec

